<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mallam Ishaku</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1806</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mallam Ishaku was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> commander who took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daura">Daura</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a> around 1806 and became its first Fulani emir. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> ruling house fled north and kept a rival court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zango">Zango</a>. Daura then became an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>, while the old dynasty was restored by the British in 1904.</p></div>
